  "notes": "FORMATION:\n{引|ひ}く (to pull) + {抜|ぬ}く (to extract) → to pull and extract\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive verb - takes を to mark the object being pulled out.\n\nBUSINESS USAGE (Sense 2):\nIn business contexts, {引|ひ}き{抜|ぬ}き is a noun meaning \"headhunting\" or \"poaching (of talent).\" The practice is common in industries with talent shortages.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {抜|ぬ}く (to pull out - simpler form)\n- {引|ひ}っこ{抜|ぬ}く (to yank out - more forceful)\n- ヘッドハンティング (headhunting - loanword)",
